<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="59412" href="schedule/2013/spring/NRES/512/59412.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2013" href="schedule/2013.xml">2013</calendarYear><term id="120131" href="schedule/2013/spring.xml">Spring 2013</term><subject id="NRES" href="schedule/2013/spring/NRES.xml">Natural Resources and Environmental Sciences</subject><course id="512" href="schedule/2013/spring/NRES/512.xml">Discussions in NRES</course></parents><sectionNumber>SSS</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Sources Sinks &amp; Sustainability</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 14-Jan-13 - 02-Apr-13.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The conceptual framework of source-sink dynamics integrates aspects of population biology and landscape ecology and has applications to habitat management and biodiversity conservation.  In this seminar, we will survey current ideas of source-sink dynamics across landscapes in relation to three main themes: 1) Source-sink theory, 2) Advances in source-sink methodology, and 3) Management based on source-sink concepts.  For graduate students or advanced undergraduates with permission of the instructor.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2013-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2013-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="CNF">Conference</type><start>04:00 PM</start><end>05:30 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>T      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>N527</roomNumber><buildingName>Turner Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Schooley" firstName="R">Schooley, R</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>